Subject: [PATCH] fix(db): viewer must not insert documents via PostgREST (RLS)

For AI #1 lane (supabase/migrations). At pin 5eacf71 security-baseline.json
records viewer: "ri" on documents (read+insert). Viewer should not write.

This patch is a migration proposal: add lf_rules guard and tighten RLS.
Apply as new migration 20261119XXXXXX_viewer_documents.sql, not as direct edit.

-- Migration: 20261119XXXXXX_viewer_documents.sql
-- Tighten `documents` browser writes to require lf_can_write(ws) not just membership.

-- 1) lf_rules: ensure documents row has allow_viewer_write = false
--    (adjust existing row if present; idempotent)
insert into lf_rules(table_name, rule)
values ('documents', jsonb_build_object('allow_viewer_write', false))
on conflict (table_name) do update
  set rule = lf_rules.rule || jsonb_build_object('allow_viewer_write', false);

-- 2) Replace viewer-insert policy: require writer role
--    Drop old permissive policy if it exists (name varies by migration)
do $$
begin
  if exists (select 1 from pg_policies where schemaname='public' and tablename='documents' and policyname='documents_viewer_insert') then
    execute 'drop policy "documents_viewer_insert" on public.documents';
  end if;
end$$;

-- Recreate with writer check (uses same lf_ws_role helper as other tables)
create policy "documents_writer_insert"
  on public.documents
  for insert
  with check (lf_can_write((data->>'workspaceId')::text));

-- 3) Also ensure viewer cannot update/delete documents they inserted
create policy "documents_writer_update"
  on public.documents
  for update
  using (lf_can_write((data->>'workspaceId')::text))
  with check (lf_can_write((data->>'workspaceId')::text));

-- Add RLS test in supabase/tests/rls.test.sql:
--   as viewer, attempt insert into documents → expect refusal (0 rows, or PGRST 403)
--   as bookkeeper, same insert → allowed (or per product decision)
-- Update security-baseline.json: tables.documents.viewer should become "r" after this migration

